In a long enough game, spells become a limited resource.
Characters forget spells after a mere 30K turns and a
spellbook is only good for a limited number of readings.
In a game over 300K turns it is quite possible to end up
with a big stack of blank spellbooks that used to be your
favorite spells, a big stack of blank spellbooks that you
dipped to ditch what you decided are worthless spells,
and you end up with more and more empty blessed magic
markers.  Blessed charging starts to be something you
spend on magic markers ...

In a long wizard game with a lot of sacfests, the create
monster spell becomes a limiting factor that comsumes
markers faster than less frequently used spells.



